{"step_index":187,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:15:20Z","input_tokens":2835,"cache_read_tokens":180058,"output_tokens":2117,"content":"# 🚀 AegisShield EDR - New Features Successfully Implemented\n\nI have implemented and verified all three requested feature sets:\n1. **Allow & Block Access Control Policy Engine**\n2. **Automated & On-Demand Email Security Reporting (SMTP)**\n3. **Network Process Intelligence & IP Origin Tracer with Genuineness Assessment**\n\n---\n\n### 🌟 New Capabilities Added\n\n#### 1. 🛡️ Allow / Block Policy Control Engine\n* [**`backend/policy_engine.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/policy_engine.py):\n  * **Allowlist (Whitelist):** Explicitly mark processes by **Name**, **Executable Path**, or **SHA256 Hash** as trusted. Whitelisted software has its threat score neutralized to 0, alerts suppressed, and is exempt from termination.\n  * **Blocklist (Blacklist):** Explicitly ban rogue software. Any process matching a blacklist rule is flagged as `CRITICAL` (Score: 100) and prioritized for termination.\n  * **IP Banning & Windows Firewall Integration:** Ban suspicious remote IP addresses. AegisShield generates an outbound block rule via Windows Firewall (`netsh advfirewall firewall add rule ...`) and flags any process attempting communication with banned IPs.\n  * **UI Controls:** 1-click `Allow` and `Block` buttons directly on every process row and threat card, plus a dedicated **Access Control & Rules** dashboard tab.\n\n#### 2. 🌐 Network Radar & IP Origin Tracer\n* [**`backend/network_tracer.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/network_tracer.py):\n  * **Network Process Auditing:** Identifies every process currently utilizing network sockets, listing local ports, remote endpoints, and connection states (`LISTEN`, `ESTABLISHED`).\n  * **Source Tracing (Reverse DNS & Geolocation):** Resolves remote IPs to hostnames via PTR records and identifies geographic location and ISP/ASN organization.\n  * **Genuineness & Reputation Classifier:**\n    * 🟢 **`GENUINE CLOUD / CDN`**: Verified major tech infrastructure (Microsoft/Azure, Google, Cloudflare, Amaz\n<truncated 2391 bytes>\nckend/detector.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/backend/detector.py): Multi-vector engine now checks policy whitelist/blacklist and banned IP communication.\n* [**`cli_scanner.py`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/cli_scanner.py): Updated with `--network`, `--rules`, `--allow`, `--block`, and `--email-report` options.\n* [**`README.md`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/README.md): Updated user documentation.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 How to Use the New Features\n\n#### In the Web Dashboard:\n1. Double-click [**`start_dashboard.bat`**](file:///c:/Users/thann/Downloads/AntiGravity/SpywareProcessMon/start_dashboard.bat) (or run `python run_server.py`) and open **`http://localhost:8888`**.\n2. **Network Radar Tab:** Click **\"Network Radar & Origin Tracer\"** to inspect all processes using the network, view remote IPs, hostnames, and genuineness badges, or click **\"Block IP\"** to ban an IP in the firewall.\n3. **Access Control Tab:** Click **\"Access Control & Rules\"** to review your whitelist, blacklist, and banned IPs, or click **\"Add Custom Rule\"**.\n4. **Email Alerts Tab:** Click **\"Email Alerts\"** (or the header **\"Email Report\"** button), enter your SMTP settings, and click **\"Send Full Report Now\"** or **\"Send Test Verification\"**.\n5. **Quick Allow / Block:** In the **Process Explorer** and **Threat Center**, click **\"Allow\"** to instantly whitelist a process or **\"Block\"** to ban it.\n\n#### From the Terminal (CLI):\n```bash\n# 1. Audit all processes using the network and trace IP origin\npython cli_scanner.py --network\n\n# 2. View all active allowlist and blocklist rules\npython cli_scanner.py --rules\n\n# 3. Whitelist (trust) a process\npython cli_scanner.py --allow internal_admin.exe\n\n# 4. Blacklist (ban) a process or remote IP\npython cli_scanner.py --block bad_tool.exe\npython cli_scanner.py --block 198.51.100.50\n\n# 5. Generate and dispatch full HTML security report to an email\npython cli_scanner.py --email-report admin@yourdomain.com\n```","thinking":"Initial analysis focuses on the policy engine and network tracer modules. The policy engine defines whitelists and blacklists to control process execution and network access. The network tracer audits network activity, mapping ports to endpoints, and classifying connections based on their nature. This suggests the system is designed for security monitoring and control.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
