{"step_index":189,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:20:27Z","input_tokens":2500,"cache_read_tokens":182955,"output_tokens":1829,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nConsidering network-wide ad blocking approaches: local DNS sinkhole servers and HTTP/HTTPS proxies. Evaluating the feasibility of a local DNS sinkhole on port 53 using tools like `dnslib` and raw sockets, or a local HTTP/HTTPS proxy. Determining if Windows permits binding to port 53 directly, or if the DNS client service is already using it.\n\n\nExploring a combined DNS ad-blocker and HTTP/HTTPS proxy approach for comprehensive network-wide filtering on Windows. This involves setting up a local DNS sinkhole (similar to AdGuard/Pi-hole) and an SNI proxy to intercept web traffic, with an option to easily enable/disable it as a system proxy via Windows settings. Blocklists from StevenBlack, EasyList, and others will be used to filter known domains. Detailed real-time logging of all browsed domains, blocking actions, and response codes, along with an analytics dashboard, are also planned.\n\n\nPlan artifact creation focuses on the ad blocker, proxy/DNS engine, analytics, and dashboard. Archiving brain files involves copying contents from the specified directory into a designated project documentation folder.\n\nComprehensive documentation requires a design and architecture document, project structure overview, code explanation, command reference, session information, prompt and response documentation, a README file, and a screenshot engine, along with a testing engine to verify functionality.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python -c \\\"\\nimport socket\\nfor port in [53, 5353, 8080, 8443, 8888, 9090]:\\n    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)\\n    try:\\n        s.bind(('127.0.0.1', port))\\n        print(f'UDP Port {port}: AVAILABLE')\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        print(f'UDP Port {port}: IN USE ({e})')\\n    finally:\\n        s.close()\\n\\n    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)\\n    try:\\n        s.bind(('127.0.0.1', port))\\n        print(f'TCP Port {port}: AVAILABLE')\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        print(f'TCP Port {port}: IN USE ({e})')\\n    finally:\\n        s.close()\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Check UDP and TCP ports availability\""}}]}
