{"step_index":201,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:22:00Z","input_tokens":3278,"cache_read_tokens":198974,"output_tokens":3429,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nInitial hypothesis is that a system proxy setup handles website traffic and filters requests against blocklists. The `traffic_logger` captures detailed browsing data, which is then aggregated by the analytics engine. The proxy controller manages the system's proxy settings, while the adblock proxy intercepts and filters web traffic.\n\n\nAdBlock Proxy uses HTTP status codes to indicate the request's fate; 403 for blocked content and 200 for allowed. The backend server (`backend/server.py`) automatically starts the proxy on port 8080 and provides a REST API to manage its functionality. The frontend introduces a new tab to control the proxy and visualize browsing activity and blocked content.\n\n\nThe system's real-time traffic log will include detailed timestamps, domains, methods, ports, and categorized badges (clean, ads, trackers). A search input and status filters will enable quick filtering by \"All\", \"Blocked Ads Only\", or \"Allowed Sites Only\". An automated testing engine is being built to comprehensively verify the AdBlocker Proxy, including port binding, blocked/allowed traffic verification, and logging accuracy.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nAegisShield - Curated Ad, Tracker, Telemetry & Malware Domain Rules\\nDerived from StevenBlack/hosts, EasyList, AdGuard DNS, and Peter Lowe's Blocklist.\\nProvides sub-domain and wildcard pattern matching with O(1) domain set lookup.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom typing import Set, Tuple, Dict, Any\\n\\n# Primary Advertising Networks & Exchanges\\nAD_DOMAINS: Set[str] = {\\n    # Google Ad Ecosystem\\n    \\\"doubleclick.net\\\", \\\"adservice.google.com\\\", \\\"pagead2.googlesyndication.com\\\",\\n    \\\"googleadservices.com\\\", \\\"tpc.googlesyndication.com\\\", \\\"partnerad.l.google.com\\\",\\n    \\\"admob.com\\\", \\\"googleads.g.doubleclick.net\\\", \\\"afs.googlesyndication.com\\\",\\n    \\n    # Major Commercial Ad Networks & Supply-Side Platforms\\n    \\\"adnxs.com\\\", \\\"ib.adnxs.com\\\", \\\"secure.adnxs.com\\\",\\n    \\\"criteo.com\\\", \\\"static.criteo.net\\\", \\\"bidder.criteo.com\\\",\\n    \\\"taboola.com\\\", \\\"trc.taboola.com\\\", \\\"cdn.taboola.com\\\",\\n    \\\"outbrain.com\\\", \\\"widgets.outbrain.com\\\", \\\"log.outbrain.com\\\",\\n    \\\"pubmatic.com\\\", \\\"ads.pubmatic.com\\\",\\n    \\\"rubiconproject.com\\\", \\\"optimized-by.rubiconproject.com\\\",\\n    \\\"openx.net\\\", \\\"us-u.openx.net\\\",\\n    \\\"casalemedia.com\\\", \\\"popads.net\\\", \\\"propellerads.com\\\",\\n    \\\"mgid.com\\\", \\\"revcontent.com\\\", \\\"adroll.com\\\", \\\"smartadserver.com\\\",\\n    \\\"bidswitch.net\\\", \\\"moatads.com\\\", \\\"yieldmo.com\\\", \\\"inmobi.com\\\",\\n    \\\"adcolony.com\\\", \\\"applovin.com\\\", \\\"unityads.unity3d.com\\\", \\\"ironsrc.com\\\",\\n    \\\"exponential.com\\\", \\\"sovrn.com\\\", \\\"media.net\\\", \\\"adtechus.com\\\",\\n    \\\"zergnet.com\\\", \\\"adblade.com\\\", \\\"sharethrough.com\\\", \\\"triplelift.com\\\",\\n    \\\"gumgum.com\\\", \\\"teads.tv\\\", \\\"conversantmedia.com\\\", \\\"clicksor.com\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# Behavioral Trackers, Analytics & Fingerprinting Endpoints\\nTRACKER_DOMAINS: Set[str] = {\\n    # Analytics & Behavioral Tracking\\n    \\\"google-analytics.com\\\", \\\"ssl.google-analytics.com\\\", \\\"analytics.google.com\\\",\\n    \\\"hotjar.com\\\", \\\"static.hotjar.com\\\", \\\"script.hotjar.com\\\",\\n    \\\"clarity.ms\\\", \\\"c.clarity.ms\\\",\\n    \\\"segment.io\\\", \\\"api.segment.io\\\", \\\"cdn.segment.\n<truncated 4178 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\thann\\\\Downloads\\\\AntiGravity\\\\SpywareProcessMon\\\\backend\\\\adblock_rules.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
